{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01SPbGHo3rbFiuKo1ovTuyVY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 8 friction points. Per skill — present candidates, ask which to grill. User said \"do all\" but each needs design decisions. Presenting tight slate first.\n\n## Candidates (architectural deepening, severity-ordered)\n\n**1. Converge bypasses the launcher seam** — `lib/loops/converge.sh` declares control but launch yields a bare CLI (`bin/almanac converge --goal …`), not a runner like ralph/harden. `cmd/converge.sh` runs the loop body itself instead of resolving config + execing a runner. Adapter shape diverges from sibling loops. **Subsumes #3, #5, #7.**\n   - **Fix:** Split `cmd/converge.sh` → thin CLI front-end (argparse + delegate to launcher) + a runner script in `bin/`, like harden. Launcher already handles role config; converge can plug in.\n\n**2. Control-file wrapper duplicated across loops** — `almanac_converge_control_file` and `almanac_harden_control_file` are mirror twins. 3rd loop = 3rd copy.\n   - **Fix:** Move to `lib/run.sh` as `almanac_loop_control_file <loop> <kind>`; both -core files call shared.\n\n**3. Auto-commit logic embedded in converge worker** — `almanac_converge_commit_agent_paths` + dirty-snapshot dance is tangled into `_run_worker_prompt`. No seam for future loops to opt in.\n   - **Fix:** Extract to `lib/commit.sh` (or `lib/run.sh`) — `almanac_loop_commit_agent_delta <paths-snapshot>`. Converge calls it; future loops too.\n\n**4. Status rendering split between registry + converge-core** — `almanac_converge_status` does custom rendering instead of using the shared hub read-views from `lib/run.sh`.\n   - **Fix:** Push converge's per-round summary fields into the run-status record contract; status renderer reads via shared `almanac_loop_read_run`.\n\n**5. Overseer verdict parser falls back to CONTINUE on malformed output** — silent failure mode. Hard-to-diagnose stalls.\n   - **Fix:** Strict parse + explicit `verdict=MALFORMED` path; surface to overseer log; default behavior configurable (continue vs. stop).\n\n**6. Role wrapper `almanac_converge_role`/`_field`** — shallow wrapper over `almanac_loop_role_config`. Harden calls shared resolver directly.\n   - **Fix:** Delete wrapper; update converge callers to use shared. Trivial.\n\n**7. Argparse divergence cmd/converge.sh vs cmd/harden.sh** — different error UX, inline `usage` calls. Low severity.\n   - **Fix:** Pick one pattern (harden's is leaner); align. Or extract `_parse_args` helper — but only if 2+ adapters justify the seam.\n\n**8. Verdict-validation duplication in tests** — `test-converge.sh` and `test-harden.sh` each roll their own verdict scaffolds.\n   - **Fix:** Shared verdict-validation helper in `lib/run.sh` + shared test scaffold. Couples with #5.\n\nOrder I'd implement: #6 (warm-up, trivial), #2 (foundation for later), #5 (correctness, narrow), #3 (extracts commit seam), #1 (the big one — restructures converge under launcher), #4 (rides on #1), #7 (alignment), #8 (rides on #5)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33876,"cache_read_input_tokens":18112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33876},"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"tools_changed","cache_missed_input_tokens":45107}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14593634-940e-4f64-9481-34cf5bee965a","uuid":"a0489523-8fce-48be-9e71-63d239dbea78","request_id":"req_011CbRHVdSDnhzktah3Jeuwh"}
